:: S: Meeting VehVeh [storylet] {"position":"6150,1525","size":"100,100"}
{=

(storylet: when
$char's VehVeh's alive is true
and $char's VehVeh's know is false
and $char's VehVeh's location is $place's sublocation and it is "Apesai Lighthouse"
and $char's VehVeh's opinion's 2nd > 20
and $char's VehVeh's arc is 1
)

(metadata:
"NPC", "VehVeh",
"title", "A Fellow Student?",
"cardDesc", "Under the aurora of the lighthouse, a woman your age is lost between the pages of a tome.",
"img", "Assets/Portraits/Girl_1.png", 
)


$cssColumnParent[

$cssColumnChild[
	$cssBox[
    	($funcImage: (passage:)'s img)
         $cssBoxItem[''(print: (passage:)'s title )''<br>(print: (passage:)'s cardDesc)]
    ]
]

$cssColumnChild[
Though you have not met her before, she is immediately familiar: Dark Nurandahid hair, fine garb, albeit plain, and a five-pointed star adorns her cap.
<br>
She must be a senior apprentice, a magus-to-be, at most a year away from journeying like you.
<br>
For now, she is hunched over a bench under pavilion, trying her best to read her book despite the rainbow light intruding upon the page. Why not study inside?
<br>
Your question is quickly answered when you hear a boy screaming, another laughing, and then a splash. Juniors. They are ungovernable anywhere, especially out here in the marches.
<br>
She flips another page and bites her thumb, not noticing you yet.
<br>
---
<ol>

<li>(link: "Approach and ask if this is where the davehmars are.")[\
	($funcNPCKnow: "VehVeh", "You've met Veh-Veh, an apprentice-magus. It's good to know another student here.")\
    (goto: "Meeting VehVeh 1a")\
]<!--[[Meeting VehVeh 1a]]-->

<li>(link: "Leave her alone.")[$funcBack]
</ol>

]<!--end child-->
]<!--end parent-->